Package: LFPM
Type: Package
Title: Adaptive L-Statistic Tests for Linear Factor Pricing Models
Version: 0.1.2
Author: Chenxi Zhao
Maintainer: Chenxi Zhao <chxzhao@mail.nankai.edu.cn>
Description: Implements ordered-sum and adaptive tests of intercepts in
    high-dimensional linear factor pricing models, with reusable R functions
    and simulation and empirical reproduction workflows for "Testing factor
    pricing restrictions in high dimensions without knowing the sparsity of
    alphas". Provides explicit bootstrap-tail and bootstrap-moment component
    calibration options. An optional Python backend preserves the empirical
    implementation's random streams and numerical conventions. Market data
    must be acquired separately from the documented external sources and are
    not distributed with the package.
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.2.0)
Imports: stats, utils, graphics, grDevices, parallel
SystemRequirements: Python 3.9 or later with NumPy, pandas, SciPy, statsmodels,
    threadpoolctl and optionally matplotlib for empirical reproduction;
    a C++ compiler and BLAS/LAPACK for the optional empirical QUIC solver
NeedsCompilation: no
